{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224943-space-question","id":1224943,"title":"Space question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-05T06:51:47-07:00","id":1224943,"title":"Space question","content":"This thought came to mind while watching <i>Interviews with Monster Girls</i> (a show I recommend). A mage uses a Space spell to give the appearance of a dullahan, a kind of Irish faerie who carries his head (or her head, there are tales of female dullahans) under one arm. Obviously, the spell will be subject to Dissonance, or just running out of Duration, but what happens when it collapses? Does the head snap back, or is there a sudden decapitation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T08:18:06-07:00","id":1224957,"title":"","content":"Well, you could certainly mimic that appearance with a sort of co-location/ban in which case when it expires your head just appears where it was all along. Space could, with weaving or similar change the position of just your head, but that's essentially just a damage spell using warp. A tiny co-location disc where your neck is could facilitate the illusion your head is separate without actually separating it as far as biology is concerned if just make it cost an extra reach or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T09:52:10-07:00","id":1224990,"title":"","content":"You'd have to make a spell for that first before it's possible to analyse the effects of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T11:51:21-07:00","id":1225044,"title":"","content":"Looking through my PDF, I'd say...<br /> <br /> Lost Your Head (Space 3, Life 2, Matter 2)<br /> Practice: Fraying<br /> Withstand: Stamina<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggest Rote Skills: Intimidation, Medicine, Occult<br /> <br /> This spell creates a Space portal over the subject's neck, allowing the person to remove their head without harm for the duration. Air, food, water, nerve signals, etc. all pass normally in both directions. The head can talk, eat, drink, and otherwise perform all the normal functions of a head, but cannot move independently. The body can be awkward to control, giving -4 to all physical tasks until the subject has had sufficient practice with this condition (the recommend rate of acclimation would be to reduce the penalty by one point each month). Normally, a Key is included to limit the passage of living matter to the subject's own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 06-05-2018, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T12:49:56-07:00","id":1225061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224943-space-question?p=1225044#post1225044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking through my PDF, I'd say...<br /> <br /> Lost Your Head (Space 3, Life 2, Matter 2)<br /> Practice: Fraying<br /> Withstand: Stamina<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggest Rote Skills: Intimidation, Medicine, Occult<br /> <br /> This spell creates a Space portal over the subject's neck, allowing the person to remove their head without harm for the duration. Air, food, water, nerve signals, etc. all pass normally in both directions. The head can talk, eat, drink, and otherwise perform all the normal functions of a head, but cannot move independently. The body can be awkward to control, giving -4 to all physical tasks until the subject has had sufficient practice with this condition (the recommend rate of acclimation would be to reduce the penalty by one point each month). Normally, a Key is included to limit the passage of living matter to the subject's own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd put it as a Space Patterning spell. It would retain the physical connection between two parts of the subject (whether it be a living being or an object; there's really no need to put a limit on that) while removing the need for a spatial connection, thereby causing it to &quot;detach&quot; while suffering no harm. Since it's not a transformation of the subject (and the &quot;detached&quot; area might be considered an Iris) there's no need to include any other Arcana. Once the duration ends, the subject's parts will reestablish their spatial connection, which in practice would teleport the parts into place, with the largest part being the spatial anchor that the rest teleports to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T12:54:24-07:00","id":1225062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224943-space-question?p=1225061#post1225061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd put it as a Space Patterning spell. It would retain the physical connection between two parts of the subject (whether it be a living being or an object; there's really no need to put a limit on that) while removing the need for a spatial connection, thereby causing it to &quot;detach&quot; while suffering no harm. Since it's not a transformation of the subject (and the &quot;detached&quot; area might be considered an Iris) there's no need to include any other Arcana. Once the duration ends, the subject's parts will reestablish their spatial connection, which in practice would teleport the parts into place, with the largest part being the spatial anchor that the rest teleports to.</div> </div> </div> </div>unless there's a distance-limiting factor, this plus some Death spells to disguise your heartbeat and breathing and make it look like a wound would be nice, gross way to infiltrate your worst enemies' stronghold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T21:25:23-07:00","id":1225167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224943-space-question?p=1225061#post1225061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd put it as a Space Patterning spell. It would retain the physical connection between two parts of the subject (whether it be a living being or an object; there's really no need to put a limit on that) while removing the need for a spatial connection, thereby causing it to &quot;detach&quot; while suffering no harm. Since it's not a transformation of the subject (and the &quot;detached&quot; area might be considered an Iris) there's no need to include any other Arcana. Once the duration ends, the subject's parts will reestablish their spatial connection, which in practice would teleport the parts into place, with the largest part being the spatial anchor that the rest teleports to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Works for me. Add a Forces spell for a &quot;cold blue flame,&quot; and you've got the whole package.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T01:00:06-07:00","id":1225190,"title":"","content":"Another idea: if you just want an &quot;Impression&quot; of a Dullahan you could use veiling to make you head appear separate from the rest of the body, though the effect would be cosmetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 06-06-2018, 04:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T02:07:58-07:00","id":1225197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224943-space-question?p=1225044#post1225044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking through my PDF, I'd say...<br /> <br /> Lost Your Head (Space 3, Life 2, Matter 2)<br /> Practice: Fraying<br /> Withstand: Stamina<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggest Rote Skills: Intimidation, Medicine, Occult<br /> <br /> This spell creates a Space portal over the subject's neck, allowing the person to remove their head without harm for the duration. Air, food, water, nerve signals, etc. all pass normally in both directions. The head can talk, eat, drink, and otherwise perform all the normal functions of a head, but cannot move independently. The body can be awkward to control, giving -4 to all physical tasks until the subject has had sufficient practice with this condition (the recommend rate of acclimation would be to reduce the penalty by one point each month). Normally, a Key is included to limit the passage of living matter to the subject's own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why Matter? Like, it probably doesn't even need Life, but Matter seems pointless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T06:09:35-07:00","id":1225233,"title":"","content":"Air, food and water are all Matter. Being able to eat, drink and breathe is important. Life for nerve signals and blood flow (I based the spell on Ban and Co-Location).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T06:37:53-07:00","id":1225242,"title":"","content":"Ban applies a supernatural effect on an area and needs other Arcana to selectively affect things under those Arcana's purviews. Your spell would either allow all of those through, or none of those through (which would be instantly lethal) in its basic form, with additional Arcana being optional modifications. But since it's an Iris (you even said it was a portal) then it would allow everything through non-selectively.<br /> When designing spells for a very specific effect (decapitation that isn't lethal) you should start with the most basic effect (severing part of a subject without damaging the subject) and extrapolate from there. Otherwise it's too easy to bring in artificial limitations (such as the spell only being able to work on the heads of living beings) or conjunctional Arcana that really should be optional (if they're needed at all).<br /> <br /> Quick edit: The reason I chose Space 4 instead of Space 3 is because it divides a subject. None of the published Space 3 effects allows that. Ban, Co-Location and Teleportation all deals with whole subjects. You can't teleport away someone's head because the entire person is the subject for the spell, hence a more advanced Practice would be required.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 06-06-2018, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T07:04:03-07:00","id":1225250,"title":"","content":"I'd put in Patterning as well as you're completely restructuring the Space component of a person's pattern to do things it just should not be able to do. I also wouldn't bother with Life or Matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T07:45:08-07:00","id":1225264,"title":"","content":"Revised. Any further commentary or suggestions?<br /> <br /> Lost Your Head (Space 4)<br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Withstand: Stamina<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggest Rote Skills: Intimidation, Medicine, Occult<br /> <br /> This spell cause the subject's head and neck to remain local in their own frame of reference while being separate in all other frames, allowing the person to remove their head without harm for the duration. Air, food, water, nerve signals, etc. all pass normally in both directions. The head can talk, eat, drink, and otherwise perform all the normal functions of a head, but cannot move independently. The body can be awkward to control, giving -4 to all physical tasks until the subject has had sufficient practice with this condition (the recommend rate of acclimation would be to reduce the penalty by one point each month).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 06-06-2018, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T07:50:43-07:00","id":1225268,"title":"","content":"Eh, just minor nitpicks, like the spell doesn't have to be limited to removing just the head, you could detach and operate any limb or organ with this spell, and I don't see the reason for talking about portals, or for imposing a penalty to physical tasks. I'd put the number of things you can &quot;detach&quot; at a number equal to Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T08:38:01-07:00","id":1225293,"title":"","content":"Make it an editable Artifact, add Forces and you too can be a Chop-Chop Human","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T08:43:17-07:00","id":1225296,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the head thing is still a needless limitation. Don't design spells for a specific use. Design spells for a basic effect that can give you what you want. You don't design as spell to turn a human into a frog. You design a spell that can turn a creature into another creature, and use that spell to turn a human into a frog.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Separation (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></i><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina or Durability<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggest Rote Skills:</b> Intimidation, Larceny, Occult<br /> When distance is a lie, physical connections no longer necessitates spatial connections. This spell causes one part of the subject per Potency to disconnect. The part is still fully functional and anything that would pass through the severed area, such as air, blood, electricity, et.c, simply continues where it would if the part was still connected to the subject. This allows a severed head to breathe, speak, and even eat (if someone were to feed it). When the spell ends the spatial separation is lost and all severed parts return to the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T08:50:42-07:00","id":1225300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224943-space-question?p=1225296#post1225296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't design spells for a specific use. Design spells for a basic effect that can give you what you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this design philosophy a bit odd; I'm accustomed to creating very specific effects when designing special powers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T09:14:35-07:00","id":1225309,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if you look at the spells in the book though they all work like that. Partly it helps to cut down on spell bloat, and partly it helps to make rotes and praxis fill more than a -very- niche function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T11:30:43-07:00","id":1225371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224943-space-question?p=1225296#post1225296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the head thing is still a needless limitation. Don't design spells for a specific use. Design spells for a basic effect that can give you what you want. You don't design as spell to turn a human into a frog. You design a spell that can turn a creature into another creature, and use that spell to turn a human into a frog.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Separation (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></i><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina or Durability<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggest Rote Skills:</b> Intimidation, Larceny, Occult<br /> When distance is a lie, physical connections no longer necessitates spatial connections. This spell causes one part of the subject per Potency to disconnect. The part is still fully functional and anything that would pass through the severed area, such as air, blood, electricity, et.c, simply continues where it would if the part was still connected to the subject. This allows a severed head to breathe, speak, and even eat (if someone were to feed it). When the spell ends the spatial separation is lost and all severed parts return to the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now it can be an overcomplicated way to have a fully-charged phone at all times if you're an Acanthus with a stick up your ass about using the Forces Arcana","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T11:34:03-07:00","id":1225374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224943-space-question?p=1225300#post1225300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find this design philosophy a bit odd; I'm accustomed to creating very specific effects when designing special powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages are not D&amp;D Wizards. As Tvtropes says, most Mage problems arise from some smart aleck getting too creative with spells","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg